# RELEASE-NOTES — Residua 0.1

English | [中文](RELEASE-NOTES.zh-CN)

Release 0.1 is the minimal self-bootstrap closure: verifiable-provenance
compilation. Given a source and an artifact, anyone can rebuild from the
committed wasm seed with a C compiler and no other toolchain, and check
byte for byte that the artifact comes from the source — trusting neither
the publisher nor a large binary toolchain.

## In this archive

- the committed `rsdc`/`rsc` wasm seeds and their 54-member source
  closure (`bootstrap/seed/stage-14274/`)
- the seed recipe (`bootstrap/seed/stage-14274/README.md`) and the C
  host bridges it needs
- the rsd chain `rsd -> rscm -> wasm` invoked as the stage host's file
  contract (`release/docs/RSD-COMMAND`)
- frozen formal semantics per layer (scm, lambda-RC, wasm0) pinned by
  content digest, as specification texts
- the language conformance corpus the bootstrap grammar was measured
  against (`release/docs/LANGUAGE` rows)
- the 0.1 performance record (`release/docs/PERF-RECORD.tsv`, form in
  `release/docs/PERF-RECORD`)
- the stranger documents: INSTALL, QUICKSTART, VERIFY-RELEASE, OVERVIEW,
  LANGUAGE, STDLIB, RSD-COMMAND, SPECS, RESIDUES, PERF-RECORD — in
  English; README and nine `release/docs/` texts (OVERVIEW, ARCHITECTURE,
