## Verification

`release/docs/VERIFY-RELEASE` is the protocol: seed digests, the
archive digest, then the full seed recipe on a clean Linux x86-64 — the recipe's rebuilt compiler images must compare
byte-identical to the committed seeds (`seed_roundtrip=2/2`).

## Stated limits of 0.1

Single-module programs (no `import`); no I/O execution layer; no proof
checking (the R-CIC checker is not in this release); no UInt64; a 4 GiB
address space; the q content-identity format is not final; no
publish/query entry for results; no importable standard library. The
bootstrap `.rsd` grammar refuses `theorem`, `axiom`, `class`, `abbrev`,
`variable`, `opaque`, `by` and `import`.

## Order after 0.1

1. R-CIC kernel + q format + Jig's publish/query entry — the first point
   a stranger can find, check and reuse another's result.
2. Programming completeness: modules, real programs, UInt64, an
   execution layer, 64-bit addressing, application suites.
3. Cheap confirmation of execution: wasm0 -> AIR -> zk.
4. Generic connectors to external semantics (K/KORE, Lean/Rocq import).

`closure_claim=0` (`release/MANIFEST.md`).
